{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Bedroom for Better Flow and Safety",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Ever wonder how to make your bedroom feel more spacious and safe? It all starts with smart planning, especially when it comes to pathway clearance. First off, grab a measuring tape and sketch out your room. Think about where you naturally walk. That's your main circulation route. Now, try placing your bed, because that's usually the biggest piece. A neat trick is to use painter's tape on the floor to outline where your furniture will go before you even move it in. Aim for about 30-36 inches of clear space beside the bed for comfy movement. For main walkways, shoot for at least 36 inches, or even more if you have two people trying to pass or if you use mobility aids. Don't forget to account for doors swinging open and closet access! If your room is on the smaller side, or has tricky angles, it might be worth bringing in a space planner or a pro to help balance safety and all your furniture pieces. They can really help make a tight space feel functional without sacrificing safety. Planning ahead really makes a difference!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
